course: dictionary
lesson: 13877
title: Words about traditions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These are its context. «At the Highland games, the men wore kilts and the pipers played loud music.» Men, pipers and Highland games are clues, so a kilt must be something special people wear at a Scottish event.
explain: Check your idea by putting it into the sentence. «Dad's kilt was made of red and green checked cloth, the same tartan as his cousins' kilts.» Tartan is the cloth, and a kilt is made from it. If you think a kilt is a pleated skirt, the sentence still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: A kilt is not just any skirt. It is a knee-length skirt with neat, even folds called pleats, usually made of tartan, and it is worn as part of Highland dress in Scotland and Ireland. Words like this tell us about a culture, the traditions of a place and its people.
fact: A kilt is a knee-length pleated skirt, usually made of tartan cloth.
fact: Men and boys traditionally wear kilts in Scotland and Ireland as part of Highland dress.
fact: Girls and women can also wear a similar pleated skirt, which is also called a kilt.
fact: Kilts are often worn at Scottish weddings, at Highland games and on Burns Night.
fact: Each tartan pattern is often linked to a clan, which is a family group.
exercise: «At the Highland games, the piper marched in a green and blue tartan kilt.» What is a kilt? | A kind of bagpipe | A dance held on Burns Night | A tall hat worn with a tartan jacket | *A knee-length pleated skirt, usually of tartan cloth
exercise: Each tartan pattern is often linked to a clan. What is a clan? | A type of Scottish music | A kind of cloth | A Highland castle with high walls | *A family group
exercise: Which country is a kilt traditionally worn in, as part of Highland dress? | *Scotland | Japan | Wales | France
test: «Mia's kilt swished as she danced at her cousin's wedding in Edinburgh.» What is a kilt? | A pair of long trousers | A tartan scarf | A type of hat | *A pleated skirt, usually of tartan cloth
test: Who can wear a kilt? | Only bagpipers | Only people in Wales | *Men, boys, girls and women | Only old men
exam: What is the best meaning of kilt? | *A knee-length pleated skirt, usually of tartan, worn as part of Highland dress | A flat cap worn at Burns Night | A Scottish dance with fast steps | A long wool coat worn in the snow
